# rsync-sbx allowlist.  Copy this file to `allowlist` in the same directory on
# the sandbox box (/opt/sbx/tools/rsync/allowlist, bound read-only into the job
# as /deskbox/tool/allowlist) and edit the entries.  The tool reads only
# `allowlist`; this .example file is a template and is never read.
#
#   <name> = [user@]<host>[:port]
#
# The source or destination names a remote side as <name>:<path>.  The name
# must match an entry below exactly.  The user and port come only from this
# file, never from the path the model writes.  No wildcards, no CIDR ranges,
# no default: an empty, missing or malformed file permits no remote host.
#
# Use an IPv4 address if the job has no /etc/resolv.conf; sbx-run does not bind
# one.  SSH expects id_ed25519 and known_hosts in this same directory.
#
# backup = ryan@backup.example.com
# nas    = 10.0.0.10:22
